[1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should I set up from the start?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [ ] [38;5;153mUnit tests (Recommended)[39m
  [38;5;246mTest runner plus a first passing fixture. The evaluator takes an injected clock, so due/overdue/snooze logic gets [39m
  [38;5;246mtested without waiting on real time.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Lint + auto-format
  [38;5;246mESLint plus Prettier on the stack's defaults. Cheap now, annoying to retrofit over existing code.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright driving a real browser to confirm toasts actually appear. Heavier; the main thing unit tests can't cover.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] None — keep it bare
  [38;5;246mNo tooling. Fastest to first code, but the time logic then has no automated verification at all.[39m
